WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.416
A real PQC migration program starts with cryptographic inventory.

2
00:00:04.416 --> 00:00:11.078
Organizations need to know where public-key cryptography is used before they can prioritize change.

3
00:00:11.078 --> 00:00:28.508
Inventory should include external services, internal services, certificates, VPNs, code signing, firmware signing, identity systems, third-party products, embedded devices, cloud services, APIs, build pipelines, and long-lived data protection workflows.

4
00:00:28.508 --> 00:00:38.036
Cryptographic agility is the ability to change algorithms, parameters, libraries, keys, and protocols without redesigning the entire system.

5
00:00:38.036 --> 00:00:40.593
Agility is not only a software feature.

6
00:00:40.593 --> 00:00:51.748
It is also procurement language, vendor management, architecture discipline, test coverage, documentation, incident response planning, and operational ownership.

7
00:00:51.748 --> 00:00:59.339
A system that cannot change cryptography safely will struggle with PQC and with future cryptographic transitions.

8
00:00:59.339 --> 00:01:03.523
Library and protocol support are necessary but not sufficient.

9
00:01:03.523 --> 00:01:17.854
HSM and KMS readiness, certificate authority support, validation expectations, interoperability testing, logging visibility, deployment sequencing, rollback planning, and compliance requirements all matter.

10
00:01:17.854 --> 00:01:29.319
Hybrid transition strategies may help manage compatibility, but they still require careful testing and clear assumptions about what protection the hybrid design provides.

11
00:01:29.319 --> 00:01:34.432
Standards become useful when they are translated into engineering roadmaps.

12
00:01:34.432 --> 00:01:44.115
A roadmap should identify priority systems, owners, dependencies, vendor commitments, test environments, rollout stages, and decision points.

13
00:01:44.115 --> 00:01:49.073
The goal is not to declare that the organization is quantum-safe overnight.

14
00:01:49.073 --> 00:01:54.728
The goal is to reduce uncertainty and build a path from inventory to tested deployment.
